From: Langsdorff <131063968+clangsdorff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 19:40:20 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 02/11] partitionmanager: update super partition size from block device

Setup_Super_Partition builds the synthetic /super entry with
Setup_Image, which leaves the size at zero for an unmounted block device
and shows 0MB on the backup screen. Call Update_Size(true) so it reads
the block device size.
---

--- a/partitionmanager.cpp
+++ b/partitionmanager.cpp
@@ -4736,6 +4736,9 @@
 	superPartition->Is_Present = true;
 	superPartition->Is_SubPartition = false;
 	superPartition->Setup_Image();
+	// Setup_Image leaves the size at zero for a block device that is never mounted, so the
+	// backup screen shows 0MB; Update_Size takes the size from the block device itself
+	superPartition->Update_Size(true);
 	Add_Partition(superPartition);
 	PartitionManager.Output_Partition(superPartition);
 }
